-- emit: a copy of a name (`backend.md` §9 item 1, amended 2026-10-02), in
-- a platform module (`platform/Copies.beni`): `made` and `other`, each
-- called once, are written where they are called, and the caller's binding
-- of what each returns is a copy of the name it returns. `item`'s reads are
-- all where it is bound, so each is that name and its binding goes; `kept`'s
-- are inside a function, so its copy stays.
import Copies
import Node


main : Node.Program
main = Node.printLines (Copies.demo ())
